0.3.0: Each release is kept beside its zips as its changes from the one before.

1. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Lines.rb: An XML file read as text: its records a line each, the bytes before the first and after the last, whatever other than a line break parts two records, and the SHA-256 of every byte read. A record running over more than one line stops it.
2. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Delta.rb: A release's changes, in ABN order: A and the record for an ABN added, C and the record for one changed, R and the ABN for one removed. Whole records rather than byte-level patches, which over 20261028 and 20261104 came to about five times the size once compressed, under git and under zstd --patch-from alike.
3. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Frame.rb: Everything in a release outside its records, file by file, with each file's record count and SHA-256. The gaps' positions are held as the distances between them, the extract putting a second carriage return after every hundredth record.
4. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/CompressedFile.rb: Lines streamed through zstd at level 19. zstd-ruby's StreamWriter flushes at every write, ending a block each time.
5. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Rebuild.rb: A release written out again from the one before it, its delta and its frame. + check(), which sets each file rebuilt against the frame's hash.
6. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Comparison.rb: + perform(), which writes the newer release's delta and frame under partial names, rebuilds the release from them, and names them only once it comes out exactly. + Comparison.pending(), the releases held whole which want comparing, oldest first, each set against the newest one before it held whole, so that a week missed or held only in part is compared across.
7. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Extract.rb: + each_member(), + each_record_line(), which stops where the ABNs do not rise.
8. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Release.rb: + whole?(), read from the recorded catalogue entry rather than from the directory, so that a zip cut short does not pass. + delta?(), + delta_path(), + frame_path(), + recorded_resources(), + EXTRACT_FORMAT.
9. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Fetch.rb: Its EXTRACT_FORMAT is Release's.
10. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Error.rb: + ExtractMalformed, + RebuildMismatch.
11. - exe/data_gov_au, test/exe/data_gov_au_test.rb: A command line is a program of its own, reading its own settings and passing them in.
12. ~ data_gov_au(.rb).gemspec: + zstd-ruby, at 1.5.6.2 or later, the first to take the compression level as a keyword. - switches.rb, - exe/data_gov_au.
13. + test/DataGovAu/ABR/CompressedFile_test.rb, Comparison_test.rb, Delta_test.rb, Frame_test.rb, Lines_test.rb, Rebuild_test.rb. ~ test/DataGovAu/ABR/Extract_test.rb, Release_test.rb: The files read as text, and whether a release is held whole and has its delta, are tested. ~ test/helper.rb: + record_line(), member_text(), abns(), whole_release(), older_files(), newer_files(), two_releases(): 168 runs.
14. ~ README.md: Releases land on Tuesdays, not Mondays. - The command, - Configuration, - From Ruby. + Settings, + Fetching, + Parsing, in the library's terms. + Releases kept as differences.
15. ~ ROADMAP.md: Releases land on Tuesdays around 21:39 UTC. - The command, + The stages. + Releases kept as differences. Its undecided items are in PROPOSED.md, which its opening names.
16. + PROPOSED.md: What is still undecided, under ROADMAP.md's headings.
17. ~ TODO: + The rebuild through the whole chain, checked against hashes its caller gives. + The zips' removal, on the caller's asking.
18. ~ DataGovAu::VERSION: /0.2.0/0.3.0/

## 20261103

0.2.0: + DataGovAu::ABR::Parser, DataGovAu::ABR::Extract: Records are read directly from a downloaded release's zips.

1. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Parser.rb: One XML file read as a stream and given up a record at a time. Ox rather than Nokogiri: Over a whole release, building every record, Ox's SAX parser takes 7 m 34 s where Nokogiri's takes 12 m 32 s. An element present and empty is kept apart from an element absent, the extract having both: A blank State comes back as the blank it is where an absent ASICNumber comes back as nil. An entity's own endorsement and each named fund it runs are kept apart, the extract putting both in DGR elements of the same name, the first carrying a status and no name and the second a name and no status. An individual's name is given up in its parts, joining being a decision for whoever asks. + error, + error_free?(), from the error attribute the schema requires of each file. + whole?(), which sets what a file gave up against the RecordCount it carries and wants its error to be none, so that a truncated file, or one reporting an error, is not taken for a smaller week.
2. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Extract.rb: A member is inflated by rubyzip as it is read and Ox is handed that stream, so neither a 477 MB zip nor one of the 605 MB XML files inside it is ever held whole. + members(), which orders the files by the numbers their names carry rather than by the names of the zips: The records are one stream sorted by ABN and the zips cut across it, so public_split_11_20 sorts first while holding the later half. The numbers are compared as numbers, since unpadded their characters would put file 2 after file 19, and the records would stop being one ascending run without anything in them saying so.
3. + lib/Thoran/String/NaturalComparison/natural_comparison.rb, lib/Thoran/Array/NaturalSort/natural_sort.rb: Taken from String#natural_comparison 0.0.1 and Array#natural_sort 0.0.1, and namespaced under Thoran. Required relatively rather than by name, so that another copy on the load path is not what the suite tests.
4. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Release.rb: + zip_paths(), read from the directory rather than from the catalogue, so that a release on disk can be parsed without going back to data.gov.au, and natural_sorted.
5. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Fetch.rb: Its extract_resources() orders by the numbers in the catalogue's own names, a tenth part otherwise coming between the first and the second. A release is named from the first of them. The comments on supporting_resources() and resources() count the list of resources among what they hold.
6. ~ lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Error.rb: + NothingToParse.
7. ~ exe/data_gov_au: + -p/--parse, which parses the newest release held and reports each file against the count it carries and any error it reports or fails to name, going nowhere near the network. + reported_duration(). Its output is written unbuffered, so that each file is reported as it is finished.
8. ~ data_gov_au(.rb).gemspec: + ox, + rubyzip, + test/fixtures.
9. + test/fixtures/20261020Public01.xml: Nine records cut from the published schema, validating against it: a sole trader with no business name and one with, a private company with no OtherEntity, an interstate record, a trading trust, a cancelled ABN, a superannuation fund, a record carrying three OtherEntity names and a DGR, and one carrying a blank State and Postcode, a family name standing alone and GST under the status NON. The DGR entries carry a status or a name rather than both together, as the extract does. GST under CAN and NON as well as ACT. An encoded ampersand and an apostrophe in two names. Its error is none, as a release's files report it.
10. + test/DataGovAu/ABR/Parser_test.rb, Extract_test.rb, test/Thoran/String/NaturalComparison/natural_comparison_test.rb, test/Thoran/Array/NaturalSort/natural_sort_test.rb. ~ test/DataGovAu/ABR/Fetch_test.rb: The halves are ordered by the numbers in their names. ~ test/exe/data_gov_au_test.rb: + Parsing. Where the settings put the data directory is tested through -p. ~ test/helper.rb: + release_holding(), fixture_records(), fixture_record(): 130 runs.
11. ~ README.md: + Parsing, + What a record comes out as, + On the parsing.
12. ~ TODO: - The parser.
13. ~ DataGovAu::VERSION: /0.1.0/0.2.0/

0.1.0: Download the current weekly ABR release.

1. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR.rb: + DataGovAu::ABR::ATTRIBUTION, required of any output which leaves the machine, the extract being published under CC BY 3.0 AU.
2. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Config.rb: The settings Fetch and Release share, given as keywords, through setters, or in a block. The API's URL and the user agent default as Catalogue's do. The data directory has no default, and is named as missing where it is first wanted, a release kept anywhere but where it was meant to be being a week lost to those held.
3. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Fetch.rb: The extract's halves are the ZIP resources of abn-bulk-extract, and its other resources the schema, the readme and a list of the resources. Its modified_on reports the latest last_modified among the halves, the other resources being republished on their own schedule. A release whose every file is held is left alone, so a second run in the same week costs one call to the catalogue and one range request.
4. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/ExtractDate.rb: A release is dated by the name of the first file inside one of its zips, read from the local file header at the start of it. The catalogue's last_modified dates its own record and moves whenever a resource is touched, so it would name a release holding nothing new; on the release first held the two differ by a day.
5. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Release.rb: A release is a directory named for the date the extract carries, holding the zips under the names data.gov.au serves them, the dataset's other resources, among them the schema and readme needed to read the zips, and the catalogue entry they were all found through.
6. + lib/DataGovAu/ABR/Error.rb: + DataGovAu::ABR::ExtractUndated.
7. + exe/data_gov_au: + abr. + -d/--data-directory, -n/--dry-run, -q/--quiet, -h/--help. Its config file is read, and the switches taken over it, a setting left blank or a switch left off leaving what lies beneath it standing. A file which is not a mapping stops the run. The data directory defaults to $XDG_DATA_HOME/data_gov_au. The catalogue's date is reported alongside the extract's own, the two differing.
8. ~ data_gov_au(.rb).gemspec: + switches.rb, + exe/data_gov_au.
9. + test/DataGovAu/ABR/Config_test.rb, ExtractDate_test.rb, Fetch_test.rb, Release_test.rb, test/exe/data_gov_au_test.rb. ~ test/helper.rb: The dataset's entry, with its halves, schema and readme. ~ test/DataGovAu/Dataset_test.rb, Resource_test.rb: 75 runs.
10. ~ DataGovAu::VERSION: /0.0.0/0.1.0/

0.0.0: A client for data.gov.au's CKAN API: a dataset found by its name or id, its resources described, and a resource downloaded once.

1. + lib/data_gov_au.rb, lib/DataGovAu/VERSION.rb.
2. + data_gov_au.gemspec, data_gov_au.rb.gemspec: The same gem, published under both names.
3. + lib/DataGovAu/Catalogue.rb: + dataset(), through package_show. The user agent and the API's URL are arguments with defaults rather than settings read from a file, a library having no machine of its own to configure. Either can also be set once it is made, or in a block.
4. + lib/DataGovAu/Dataset.rb: + name, title, organisation, licence, modified_at, resources, to_h. CKAN gives its times without a zone, and they are read as UTC.
5. + lib/DataGovAu/Resource.rb: + download(), written to a .partial file and renamed into place once whole, so that an interrupted download leaves nothing which would pass for the file, and stopping upon a body other than the length the catalogue reports. + first_bytes(), which asks by range and stops upon anything but 206, holding the whole body being what asking by range is meant to avoid. + held_at?(). + filename, taken from the URL, the resource's own name being prose.
6. + lib/DataGovAu/Error.rb: + DataGovAu::Error, CatalogueUnavailable, DownloadFailed.
7. + test/DataGovAu/Catalogue_test.rb, Dataset_test.rb, Resource_test.rb: 32 runs.
